{
  "title": "What time is it? — and one twist on \"half\"",
  "title_target": "Котра година? — Kotra hodyna?",
  "goal": "Tell the time, make plans to meet, and learn the one twist English speakers must watch: Ukrainian \"half three\" means 2:30, counting toward the next hour, just as German *halb drei* does.",
  "bekal": [
    "ask and tell the time",
    "use о + the ordinal form to make plans",
    "say half past and quarter past",
    "name the parts of the day",
    "say what time something starts and ends"
  ],
  "dialogs": [
    {
      "title": "Діалог — Making plans between two classes",
      "intro": "Andriy and Ani arrange a time to meet. Notice the two different forms of the hour: **третя** to name the time, and **о третій** to say at that time.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Андрій:",
          "text": "[Ані|A-nee], [котра|kot-RA] [година|ho-DI-na]?",
          "id": "Ani, what time is it?",
          "literal": "Ani, which — hour?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Пів|Peev] [на|na] [третю|TREH-tyoo].",
          "id": "Half past two.",
          "literal": "half — toward — the-third."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Андрій:",
          "text": "[Вже|Vzheh]? [А|A] [коли|ko-LI] [починається|po-chi-NA-yeh-tsya] [твоя|tvo-YA] [пара|PA-ra]?",
          "id": "Already? When does your class start?",
          "literal": "already? and — when — begins — your — class?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[О|O] [третій|TREH-teey]. [У|OO] [мене|MEH-neh] [ще|shcheh] [п'ятнадцять|pyat-NAD-tsyat'] [хвилин|khvi-LIN].",
          "id": "At three. I still have fifteen minutes.",
          "literal": "at — the-third. at — me — still — fifteen — minutes."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Андрій:",
          "text": "[А|A] [коли|ko-LI] [закінчується|za-KEEN-choo-yeh-tsya]?",
          "id": "And when does it end?",
          "literal": "and — when — ends?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[О|O] [пів|peev] [на|na] [п'яту|PYA-too].",
          "id": "At half past four.",
          "literal": "at — half — toward — the-fifth."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Андрій:",
          "text": "[Тоді|To-DEE] [зустрінемось|zoost-REE-neh-mos'] [о|o] [шостій|SHOS-teey]?",
          "id": "Then shall we meet at six?",
          "literal": "then — we-will-meet — at — the-sixth?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Краще|KRA-shcheh] [о|o] [сьомій|SYO-meey]. [Мені|Meh-NEE] [треба|TREH-ba] [в|v] [бібліотеку|beeb-lee-o-TEH-koo].",
          "id": "Better at seven. I need to go to the library.",
          "literal": "better — at — the-seventh. to-me — need — to — library (accusative)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Андрій:",
          "text": "[Добре|DOB-reh], [о|o] [сьомій|SYO-meey]. [Де|Deh]?",
          "id": "OK, at seven. Where?",
          "literal": "good, at — the-seventh. where?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Біля|BEE-lya] [метро|met-RO]. [Тільки|TEEL'-ki] [не|neh] [запізнюйся|za-PEEZ-nyooy-sya]!",
          "id": "By the metro. Just don't be late!",
          "literal": "near — metro. only — don't — be-late!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Андрій:",
          "text": "[Я|Ya] [ніколи|nee-KO-li] [не|neh] [запізнююсь|za-PEEZ-nyoo-yoos'].",
          "id": "I'm never late.",
          "literal": "I — never — not — am-late."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Вчора|VCHO-ra] [ти|ti] [запізнився|za-PEEZ-niv-sya] [на|na] [двадцять|DVAD-tsyat'] [хвилин|khvi-LIN].",
          "id": "Yesterday you were twenty minutes late.",
          "literal": "yesterday — you — were-late (past m) — by — twenty — minutes."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "**Пів на третю means 2:30, not 3:30.** Literally \"half toward the third\": the half hour on the way to three. ⚠️ English *half past two* counts from the hour just gone, so fight the urge to say *пів на другу*. (German *halb drei* and Dutch *half drie* work exactly like Ukrainian.)",
        "**The word година is feminine, so the hour uses feminine ordinal numbers.** *Перша*, *друга*, *третя*, *четверта*, *п'ята*, not *один*, *два*, *три*. You will never hear *три година*.",
        "**To name the time: the basic form. To say at that time: о + місцевий (locative).** *Третя година* (three o'clock) versus *о третій* (at three). The ending changes to **-ій**, and the word *година* is usually dropped.",
        "**Об, not о, before одинадцятій.** Like з/із/зі, this is purely for ease of pronunciation: **об одинадцятій**, **о дванадцятій**. Only one word is affected, and if you forget, no one will misunderstand you.",
        "**Ukraine also uses the twenty-four-hour clock, especially for timetables.** Trains, cinemas, and class schedules use the digital form: *чотирнадцята тридцять* (14:30). In everyday conversation people still say *пів на третю*.",
        "**Пара is a university class period, not a \"pair\".** One *пара* = two back-to-back lessons, about ninety minutes. The word is used across Ukrainian campus life, and you won't find it in a tourist phrasebook.",
        "**Запізнюватися is a reflexive verb (-ся), and its past tense follows gender.** Ani says *ти запізнився* to Andriy. To a woman it would be *запізнилася*. The past tense is covered fully in Unit 14; for now just notice the ending."
      ],
